.TH VM-CONFIG 5 "2026" "vm-manager" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
vm-config \- configuration file for vm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vm/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The optional TOML configuration file for
.BR vm (1),
at
.I ~/.config/vm/config.toml
when
.I XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset. Omitted settings take their defaults. An unreadable file, invalid
TOML or an unknown setting is an error.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.BR catalogue_url " (string)"
The gzipped tar
.B vm update
fetches. Defaults to the project's repository on GitHub.
.TP
.BR catalogue_path " (string)"
The directory within that archive holding the entries. Default
.BR catalogue .
.TP
.BR auto_pull " (boolean)"
Whether
.B vm run
fetches an image that is not held. Default
.BR true .
When
.BR false ,
a missing image is an error unless
.B \-\-pull
says otherwise.
.TP
.BR add_ssh_config " (boolean)"
Whether
.B vm run
acts as though
.B \-\-add\-ssh\-config
were given. Default
.BR false .
Images without cloud-init get no entry, and
.B \-\-no\-ssh\-config
overrides it. Existing machines are unaffected; use
.B vm start
to change them.
.TP
.BR default_user " (string)"
The account
.B vm run
creates when
.B \-\-user
is not given. The value
.B $USER
means the login name of the user running
.BR vm .
Default
.BR vm .
.SH EXAMPLE
.RS
.nf
catalogue_url = "https://mirror.example.com/vm/catalogue.tar.gz"
catalogue_path = "catalogue"
auto_pull = false
add_ssh_config = true
default_user = "$USER"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vm (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
